rts intellectual merit and the knowledge frontier in AI safety. While it adds early-stage rigor, this prevents \"black box\" deployments that are impossible to scientifically audit post-hoc.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (e.g., 85-90). It's a standard engineering practice applied to R&D; while not a \"breakthrough\" research project itself, it provides the infrastructure necessary for high-impact scientific results in high-risk AI.\n\n    *   ID: P2096\n    *   Rationale: [As drafted]\n    *   Decision: approve\n    *   Promise: 85",
