d on regulatory requirements signals maturity and professional responsibility to partners and regulators.\n    *   *Resource Efficiency:* The proposal argues that it converts \"compliance overhead\" into \"first-class debugging asset.\" From a management perspective, this is highly attractive because it justifies the cost of implementing Article 12 by providing tangible R&D value (faster iteration).\n\n    *   Is there a risk? Replaying data in a sandbox might involve PII or sensitive data. However, as an *internal developer tool* for prototypes, the primary goal is debugging and compliance verification.\n    *   Does it fulfill Article 12? Yes, it operationalizes the logs required by Art 12(3).\n\n    *   *Rationale:* This proposal effectively transforms a mandatory regulatory burden into a high-value engineering asset, ensuring that our record-keeping for high-risk systems is not only compliant but operationally verifiable. It directly addresses the traceability requirements of Recital 71 and Article 12 by making logs actionable for both audit and debugging.\n    *   *Decision:* approve.\n    *   *Promise:* 95 (Very high because it aligns compliance with R&D utility).",
