ess Art 12? Yes.\n    *   Does it address Recital 71? Yes.\n    *   Is it actionable? Yes (work with IT, provision storage, build interface).\n    *   Is it necessary? Yes. If logs are just written to local files on a server that gets wiped every 30 days or is inaccessible during an audit, the institution has failed Article 12 and Recital 71.\n\n    *   Rationale: This platform directly addresses the \"lifetime\" storage and retrieval mandates of Article 12 and Recital 71, mitigating the risk of severe regulatory penalties for lack of traceability. It transforms a technical logging requirement into an institutional capability for audit-readiness.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: Very high (95+). This is fundamental infrastructure; without it, \"logging\" is just data generation without record-keeping.",
