or.\n    *   It's a low-cost (one sprint), high-utility implementation that supports the long-term validity of our research findings when applied in \"high-risk\" settings.\n\n    *   Rationale: Maintaining interpretable log schemas is essential for longitudinal study and reproducibility, ensuring that operational data remains scientifically useful as models evolve.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (around 85-90) because it's a fundamental prerequisite for any serious scientific monitoring of AI systems, though it's more \"engineering\" than \"frontier research.\"",
