h: Shifts the burden from individual developers to a central platform.\n        *   Enforcement: CI check ensures no model \"ships\" without logging, reducing the risk of human error/oversight.\n        *   Scalability: Middleware allows for updates to what is being logged across all systems simultaneously if the regulation's interpretation changes.\n    *   *Cons:*\n        *   Potential performance overhead (function-call level logging).\n        *   Risk of \"noise\" (logging everything but not specifically what Article 12 requires, though the proposal mentions \"required events\").\n\n    *   The proposal directly addresses the core requirement of Article 12 (technical capability for automatic recording) and mitigates the risk of non-compliance during the development lifecycle. It aligns perfectly with the goal of institutional survival and regulatory compliance by making logging a mandatory, automated part of the pipeline.",
